n': 'runEndIndex equals the series end. Strategy opens a position on the last bar. Because the position is still open and we are at the series end, the extra‑bars loop runs, finds a closing signal on the first extra bar, executes it and breaks. The final record is closed.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'strategy', 'value': 'mockStrategyOpenAtEndNoCloseAfter'}, {'parameter': 'tradeType', 'value': 'TradeType.SELL'}, {'parameter': 'amount', 'value': 'Num.valueOf(2)'}, {'parameter': 'startIndex', 'value': '0'}, {'parameter': 'finishIndex', 'value': 'barSeries.getEndIndex() - 2'}], 'expected': 'tradeExecutionModel.execute is called once (open at runEndIndex); returned TradingRecord is NOT closed (open position remains) because runEndIndex != series end, so extra‑bars block is skipped', 'description': 'The run finishes before the series end, leaving an open position. The condition `runEndIndex == barSeries.getEndIndex()` is false, therefore the extra‑bars loop is not entered and the position stays open.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'strategy', 'value': 'mockStrategyOperatesOnlyWithinBounds'}, {'parameter': 'tradeType', 'value': 'TradeType.BUY'}, {'parameter': 'amount', 'value': 'Num.valueOf(3)'}, {'parameter': 'startIndex', 'value': '5'}, {'parameter': 'finishIndex', 'value': '10'}], 'expected': 'tradeExecutionModel.execute is called exactly once at i=7 (the only index where strategy.shouldOperate returns true); returned TradingRecord is open (single entry trade, no exit) because no closing signal is given within the run range and runEndIndex != series end', 'description': 'Both startIndex and finishIndex are inside the series, testing that `runBeginIndex = max(startIndex, seriesBegin)` and `runEndIndex = min(finishIndex, seriesEnd)` are applied correctly. Strategy signals an operation only on index 7, opening a trade that never closes within the provided range.'}]}]
